<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="AZD: Support" id="Azd-Reference-And-Support">

    <primary-label ref="azd"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Report a bug: <a href="https://github.com/edgafner/dorkag/issues">DORKAG issue tracker</a></p>
        <p>Usage statistics: <ui-path>Settings | Version Control | AZD | Preferences</ui-path></p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Report AZD bugs, request features, contact the developer, and learn what data AZD sends.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Report a bug, request a feature, contact the developer, and read about privacy.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Get support for the AZD Azure DevOps plugin for JetBrains IDEs: report bugs, request features,
        contact the developer and control usage statistics.</web-summary>

    <p>
        Before you report a problem, check <a href="Azd-FAQ.topic">FAQ and troubleshooting</a>.
    </p>

    <include from="common-support.topic" element-id="support-content"/>

    <chapter title="Report an IDE error" id="report-exception">
        <p>
            When the IDE shows an error that comes from AZD, click <control>Report Exception</control> in the error dialog.
            The browser opens a new GitHub issue with the error details filled in.
            Review the text, remove anything you do not want to share, and submit it.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Privacy and usage statistics" id="privacy">
        <p>
            By default, AZD sends anonymous usage statistics only for Microsoft sign-in: an event when a sign-in starts, succeeds or fails.
            To stop them, clear <control>Share anonymous usage statistics</control> in
            <ui-path>Settings | Version Control | AZD | Preferences</ui-path>.
        </p>
        <p>
            AI features send content to the AI provider you select.
            For how the built-in AZD provider handles your data, see <a href="Azd-AI.topic" anchor="ai-privacy">AI and privacy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
            Read the full <a href="privacy-policy.topic">privacy policy</a> and the <a href="terms-of-service.topic">terms of service</a>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <seealso>
